{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>והיה אם לא תשמע etc.</b> The verse conditions on three things: study of Torah, observance of negative commandments, and fulfillment of positive commandments — for all three must be together. The intention is that even if he studied Torah but did not observe, or if he observed but did not perform, or if he performed both of them yet neglected Torah study — the curses, may the Merciful One save us, will come upon him, as will be explained regarding each one of them, the punishment for each one individually. And He began with the punishment for neglect of Torah study and said <b>ארור אתה בעיר etc.</b> until the statement ״ועד אבדך מהר״, and concluded by saying <b>מפני רע מעלליך אשר עזבתני.</b> See now that the severe curses up to this point are against abandonment of Torah, for one who abandons Torah is like one who abandons HaShem. And so you will find that HaShem was so insistent about abandonment of Torah, saying (Jeremiah 9:11) ״על מה אבדה הארץ ויאמר ה׳ על עזבם את תורתי״ — and it is His saying here <b>ועד אבדך מהר מפני רע מעלליך אשר עזבתני.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:35.601873577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}